This project adapts both upstreams to the Oh My Pi (OMP) coding agent as a
native TypeScript extension. It replaces neither upstream's host layer; the
"Not ported" list below records what has no OMP equivalent.

Ported / adapted modules (mapping to upstream sources):

  dsh-purge:
  upstream lib/rules.js               -> src/rules/store.ts
                                         src/rules/activate.ts
                                         src/rules/cwd-scan.ts
  upstream lib/net-scope.js           -> src/gate/net-scope.ts
                                         src/gate/hooks.ts
  upstream lib/capability-protocol.js -> src/capability.ts
  upstream lib/table-key.js           -> src/inject/crypto.ts
  upstream lib/table-read.js          -> src/inject/crypto.ts
  upstream lib/core.js
    (normalizeOverride / hashOverride
     / resolveInjectText / readPromptInjectFileSync)
                                      -> src/inject/resolve.ts
                                         src/paths.ts
  upstream lib/default-prompt-inject.zh.md
                                      -> src/inject/default-prompt.zh.md
                                         (sealed into src/inject/slot-table.ts)

  pi-purge:
  /purge command + append/replace/strict composition
                                      -> src/mode.ts
                                         src/command/purge.ts
  per-session toggle / purge status   -> src/command/purge.ts
                                         src/mode.ts

Not ported (DSH-specific, no OMP equivalent):
  host JS source patching (ALL_PATCHES), shim injection, host restart,
  update checks, the Cordis web/desktop dock UI.

